// ex_ty -- the C type of an expression node.
//
// The emitter needs this before it can emit anything: the width of a load,
// whether a division is `/` or `udiv`, how far a pointer addition scales, and
// whether a result has to be wrapped back to 32 bits all come from the type,
// and C's front end has already thrown that information away by the time the
// AST exists. So it is recomputed here, on demand, from the same node ids the
// text emitter is walking.
//
// The dispatch is a lazy chain -- one node kind per function, `else` hands on.
// It has to be lazy: an eager chain would evaluate every arm for every node,
// and every arm recurses into the children, which is exponential in the depth
// of the expression.

ex_ty(int id) {
  int ty = 0;
  if(k_of(id) == "num") {
    ty = num_ty(id);
  } else {
    ty = ety2(id);
  }
} return int ty;
given txt_fixture (0):(0) then calls ety2:(0)
given txt_fixture (5):(0) then calls ety2:(5)

ety2(int id) {
  int ty = 0;
  if(k_of(id) == "var") {
    string name = s_of(id);
    ty = local_ty(name);
  } else {
    ty = ety3(id);
  }
} return int ty;
given txt_fixture (0):(0) then calls ety3:(0)
given txt_fixture (5):(0) then calls ety3:(5)

ety3(int id) {
  int ty = 0;
  if(k_of(id) == "bin") {
    ty = bin_ty(id);
  } else {
    ty = ety4(id);
  }
} return int ty;
given txt_fixture (0):(0) then calls ety4:(0)
given txt_fixture (5):(0) then calls ety4:(5)
